{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     navbar/theme-toggle — the two-state switch for the bar.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     The bar gets the switch because it shows BOTH states and which one is
     current, rather than asking you to infer the current mode from the icon
     of the other one. The three-way Light · Auto · Dark control lives in the
     sheet, where there is room for the honest form.

     The knob's position is decided in CSS from data-theme, which
     partials/theme-init.hbs sets before the first paint — so it is right in
     the first painted frame, before nav.js has run.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<button type="button" class="ns-themeswitch" role="switch" aria-checked="false"
        aria-label="{{t "Dark mode"}}" data-ns-theme-toggle>
    <span class="ns-themeswitch__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</button>
